				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$\infty $\end{document}∞. Thus, the proximal and distal limits of integration have to be selected (e.g., Bonadonna and Costa 2012) (Daggitt et al. 2014).

Of the three fitting methods, the Weibull model was proposed more recently as it combines the advantage of the exponential model being integrable between 0 and \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
